<tei:div corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:prayer:amidah/uvekhen_ten_pachdekha"><tei:pb n="658" ed="1949 rosh hashana and erev yom kippur" facs="https://archive.org/download/PhilipBirnbaumHaSiddurHaShalemTheDailyPrayerBook1949/page/n682_medium.jpg"/><tei:p>Now, Lord our God, put thy awe upon all whom thou hast made, thy dread upon all whom thou hast created; let thy works revere thee, let all thy creatures worship thee; may they all blend into one brotherhood to do thy will with a perfect heart. For we know, Lord our God, that thine is dominion, power and might; thou art revered above all that thou hast created.</tei:p></tei:div>
